        "text": "On a Mac, Docker stores components in two different \"Library\" locations. If you are looking specifically for the **system-level** `/Library` folder (available to all users), the"
      }, {
        "text": " folders are primarily used for background services and privileged helpers.\n\n### 1. System Library: `/Library`\nThe"
      }, {
        "text": " following paths are where Docker stores its system-wide background components:\n\n*   **Privileged Helpers:** `/Library/"
      }, {
        "text": "PrivilegedHelperTools/`\n    *   Look for files like `com.docker.vmnetd` and "
      }, {
        "text": "`com.docker.socket`. These allow Docker to manage networking and the system socket.\n*   **Launch Daemons:**"
      }, {
        "text": " `/Library/LaunchDaemons/`\n    *   Look for `com.docker.vmnetd.plist"
      }, {
        "text": "` or `com.docker.socket.plist`. These tell macOS how to start the Docker background services.\n*   **"
      }, {
        "text": "Application Support:** `/Library/Application Support/com.docker.docker/`\n    *   This folder sometimes contains system"
      }, {
        "text": "-wide configuration files like `registry.json` or certificates.\n\n---\n\n### 2. User Library: "
      }, {
        "text": "`~/Library` (Most common)\nIf you are looking for your **actual Docker data** (images, containers, and"
      }, {
        "text": " volumes), it is located in your **user\u0027s** Library, not the system one. To get there, open Finder"
      }, {
        "text": ", press `Cmd + Shift + G`, and paste:\n\n`~/Library/Containers/com.docker.docker/Data"
      }, {
        "text": "/vms/0/data/`\n\nInside this folder, you will see a large file named **`Docker.raw"
      }, {
        "text": "`** or **`Docker.qcow2`**. This file is a virtual disk that contains your entire Docker environment.\n\n###"
      }, {
        "text": " Summary Table\n| Data Type | Path |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Containers \u0026 Images** |"
      }, {
        "text": " `~/Library/Containers/com.docker.docker/Data/vms/0/data/Docker.raw"
      }, {
        "text": "` |\n| **Privileged Services** | `/Library/PrivilegedHelperTools/com.docker.vmnetd"
      }, {
        "text": "` |\n| **Startup Plists** | `/Library/LaunchDaemons/com.docker.vmnetd.plist"
      }, {
        "text": "` |\n| **Config \u0026 Metadata** | `~/.docker/` (hidden folder in your Home directory) |\n|"
      }, {
        "text": " **Application Logs** | `~/Library/Logs/Docker Desktop/` |\n\n**Note:** If you are trying to free"
      }, {
        "text": " up space, do not delete files in `/Library` manually. Instead, use the **\"Troubleshoot\"** (bug"
      }, {
        "text": " icon) menu within the Docker Desktop app to \"Clean / Purge data\" or \"Uninstall.\""
