        "text": "If you’ve already deleted Docker and the `Docker.raw` file, the \"hidden space\" you are still seeing is likely caused by one of two things: **APFS Local Snapshots"
      }, {
        "text": "** (the most common reason) or **Docker leftovers** in other hidden folders.\n\n### 1. The Most"
      }, {
        "text": " Likely Culprit: APFS Local Snapshots\nWhen you delete a massive file (like `Docker.raw`), macOS often doesn"
      }, {
        "text": "\u0027t actually release the disk space immediately. Instead, it \"locks\" those blocks in a **Local Snapshot** so that"
      }, {
        "text": " Time Machine can restore them if needed. \n\nEven if you don\u0027t use an external backup drive, macOS creates"
      }, {
        "text": " these snapshots automatically. The space is marked as \"Purgeable,\" but it won\u0027t show up as \"Free\" in"
      }, {
        "text": " many views.\n\n**How to fix it:**\n1.  Open **Terminal**.\n2.  List your"
      }, {
        "text": " current snapshots by typing:\n    ```bash\n    tmutil listlocalsnapshots /\n    ```\n3.  If"
      }, {
        "text": " you see a list of dates, you can force macOS to delete them and reclaim the space immediately by running:\n    ```bash"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    sudo tmutil thinlocalsnapshots / 9999999999 4\n    ```\n"
      }, {
        "text": "    *(You will need to enter your Mac password. This command \"thins\" the snapshots to free up as much space"
      }, {
        "text": " as possible.)*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Manual Cleanup of Docker Leftovers\nDocker leaves files in several other"
      }, {
        "text": " hidden locations besides the main `Library` folder. If you just dragged the app to the Trash, these are still on"
      }, {
        "text": " your disk:\n\nOpen **Terminal** and run these commands to remove any remaining Docker data (Copy and paste one by one):\n\n"
      }, {
        "text": "```bash\n# Configuration and Build Cache\nrm -rf ~/.docker\n\n# Metadata and Sockets\nrm -rf ~/Library/"
      }, {
        "text": "Group\\ Containers/group.com.docker\n\n# Application Support\nrm -rf ~/Library/Application\\ Support/Docker"
      }, {
        "text": "\\ Desktop\n\n# Caches\nrm -rf ~/Library/Caches/com.docker.docker\n\n# Logs\nrm"
      }, {
        "text": " -rf ~/Library/Logs/Docker\\ Desktop\n\n# Preferences\nrm -f ~/Library/Preferences/com.docker"
      }, {
        "text": ".docker.plist\nrm -f ~/Library/Saved\\ Application\\ State/com.electron.docker-frontend."
      }, {
        "text": "savedState\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Check for \"Ghost\" Virtual Machines\nIf you ever used alternative"
      }, {
        "text": " Docker tools (like **Colima**, **OrbStack**, or **Minikube**), they create their own massive disk"
      }, {
        "text": " images in different hidden folders.\n\n*   **Colima:** Check `~/.colima`\n*   **OrbStack"
      }, {
        "text": ":** Check `~/Library/Application Support/OrbStack`\n*   **Minikube:** Check `~/.minikube"
      }, {
        "text": "`\n\n---\n\n### 4. How to \"See\" the Hidden Space\nIf the space still isn\u0027t back"
      }, {
        "text": ", you can use the Terminal to find exactly which folder is the problem. Run this command to see the size of all"
      }, {
        "text": " folders in your User Library (it may take a minute to calculate):\n\n```bash\ndu -sh ~/Library/*"
      }, {
        "text": " | sort -h\n```\n\n**Look for any line ending in \"G\" (Gigabytes).** This will tell you exactly"
      }, {
        "text": " which folder is still hogging your space.\n\n**Final Tip:** Don\u0027t forget to **Empty the Trash**"
      }, {
        "text": " and **Restart your Mac**. macOS sometimes requires a reboot to recalculate the \"Available Space\" accurately after a large deletion."
